  "interpretationGuard": [
    "REL_INC is frozen before this value-specific rank measurement.",
    "The target interaction dimension is rank([affine,y0,y1])-rank(affine), so it counts only independent scalar outcome directions not already carried by the affine component model.",
    "This does not identify a closed-form syndrome function; it establishes how many GF(2) scalar correction bits such a function must supply on each complete carrier.",
    "A zero-dimensional target quotient means the scalar value is already affine even if unused structural quadratic directions exist.",
    "A one-dimensional target quotient means a single GF(2) interaction syndrome suffices for the two-bit W/D/L encoding after affine decoding.",
    "No standard-7x6 claim follows."
  ]
